<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.keel.serve.paperforward</string>

    <!-- NOTE ON COMMENT STYLE, and it is load bearing. XML forbids a DOUBLE HYPHEN inside a
         comment, which rules out writing any of keel's long options in prose here: the first
         draft of this file said "keel open port" with the option spelled out and every one of
         the four plists failed to parse. So this comment names options in words. The rest of the
         repo separates asides with a double hyphen; com.keel.live.plist carries the same warning
         for the same reason. tests/test_serve_agents.py parses these with a STRICT parser to
         keep it true. Do not "fix" the punctuation back.

         The paper-forward console (config.paperforward.yaml with the default keel.db).

         WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not a detector and it places nothing. The four
         com.keel.{live,paperforward,paper-hourly,paper-equities} agents run the CYCLES on their
         own schedules; this one only serves the read-only view of what they recorded. Two jobs
         per profile, deliberately: a console that crashed must not take the trading agent with
         it, and an agent mid-cycle must not be restarted because a browser tab died.

         WHY RunAtLoad AND KeepAlive, which are two different promises. RunAtLoad starts it at
         login or boot. KeepAlive restarts it if it exits for any reason: a crash, an OOM kill, a
         stray signal. Neither implies the other, and a file carrying only the first is the shape
         that looks correct until something dies at 3am. Stop it deliberately with
         `launchctl bootout gui/$(id &#45;u)/com.keel.serve.paperforward`; a plain `launchctl stop` is undone by
         KeepAlive within seconds, which is the point.

         THE COST OF KeepAlive, stated rather than discovered. A server that cannot BIND exits
         non-zero at once, and launchd relaunches it on its throttle (10s by default) forever,
         appending to the log each time. That is what a port collision looks like from the
         outside, and `launchctl print gui/$(id &#45;u)/com.keel.serve.paperforward` reports the exit status. Each
         console pins its own port below, so a collision cannot happen between keel's own jobs.

         HOW TO GET IN. This process prints its URL, carrying a one-time session token, to
         StandardOutPath, where nobody is reading. Do not grep the log for it. Run keel's open
         command from the deployment directory, giving it this job's port (8766); it reads the
         record a detached server leaves (mode 0600, deleted on shutdown) and opens the browser.
         See keel/web/runtime.py for why a detached server may leave that record and an
         interactive one may not. The token is new on every restart, so each KeepAlive relaunch
         invalidates open tabs, and the open command is how you come back.

         WHY THE WRAPPER AND NOT THE keel BINARY DIRECTLY. The database option defaults to
         keel.db, so a plist spelling the arguments itself could serve the PAPER ledger under
         this profile's name and be entirely convincing about it. keel-paper pins config and
         database together as a pair, which is the footgun it was written to remove. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/elmehdiaitbrahim/keel/keel-paper</string>
        <string>serve</string>
        <string>--port</string>
        <string>8766</string>
        <string>--no-open</string>
    </array>

    <!-- No browser at startup. At boot there may be no GUI session at all, and a window nobody
         asked for is not how a background service should announce itself. -->

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/elmehdiaitbrahim/keel</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/elmehdiaitbrahim/keel/logs/keel-serve-paperforward.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/elmehdiaitbrahim/keel/logs/keel-serve-paperforward.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
